# Zybble — environment variables

Copy to `.env.local` for development, and set the same keys in Vercel for
production. **Every secret is server-only.** Nothing marked `NEXT_PUBLIC_` may
hold a secret: those values are inlined into the browser bundle.

The app boots without any of these set — every page renders an honest empty or
unavailable state, and `/api/health` reports exactly what is missing. See
`LAUNCH_BLOCKERS.md`.

## Required for real payments and creator payouts

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` | server | Public key id handed to Razorpay Checkout. Safe to expose as an id. |
| `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` | **secret** | Never leaves the server. Used for signature checks and every Razorpay API call. |
| `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | **secret** | Used for HMAC-SHA256 verification of the raw webhook body. |
| `PAYOUT_DETAILS_ENCRYPTION_KEY` | **secret** | 32-byte key (64 hex chars or 44-char base64) used for AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption of creator UPI IDs and bank account numbers before storage in Postgres. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`. |

Without the three Razorpay keys, `/api/checkout` returns `503 payments_unavailable`
and paid courses cannot be bought. Free enrolment still works.
Without `PAYOUT_DETAILS_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, saving or revealing creator payout
destinations fails closed on the server.

## Database and authentication

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | public | Project URL. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` | public | The new-style publishable key. |
| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` | **secret** | Server only. Bypasses RLS — used by the payment, webhook and outbox paths that must write across users. Never import it into a component. |

## Site

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` | public | Canonical origin, e.g. `https://zybble.in`. Used for email links and post-auth redirects. |

## Video (Bunny Stream)

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `BUNNY_STREAM_LIBRARY_ID` | server | The library videos are created in. |
| `BUNNY_STREAM_API_KEY` | **secret** | API key for uploads, status and webhook signing. |
| `BUNNY_STREAM_TOKEN_AUTH_KEY` | **secret** | Signs playback tokens (`SHA256(token + videoId + expiry)`). |

## Files (Cloudflare R2, private)

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `R2_ACCOUNT_ID` | server | |
| `R2_BUCKET_NAME` | server | |
| `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | **secret** | |
| `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | **secret** | |
| `R2_S3_ENDPOINT` | server | Defaults to `https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com`. |

The bucket must have public access **disabled**. Thumbnails and avatars are
streamed through `/api/media/[kind]`; course resources are issued as short-lived
pre-signed URLs only after an entitlement check.

## Email (Resend)

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | **secret** | |
| `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL` | server | Must be on a domain you have verified with Resend. |

Transactional mail is outbox-backed: writes land in `email_outbox` first and a
dispatcher sends them. Drain it with `POST /api/email/outbox` (moderator or
admin only) from a cron job.

## AI (OpenRouter → DeepSeek)

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | **secret** | Required. Get one at <https://openrouter.ai/keys>. |
| `OPENROUTER_MODEL` | server | Defaults to `deepseek/deepseek-chat`. Any OpenRouter slug works. |
| `OPENROUTER_SITE_URL` | server | Sent as `HTTP-Referer` for OpenRouter attribution. |
| `OPENROUTER_APP_NAME` | server | Defaults to `Zybble`. |

Zybble AI answers through **DeepSeek**, reached with a single OpenRouter key —
no separate DeepSeek account, and switching models later is one variable.

Replies stream to the browser token by token. Course suggestions are read from
a `SLUGS:` trailer the model appends, and every slug is re-resolved against the
published catalog before a card is rendered, so a made-up course is dropped
rather than shown.

Without a key the chatbot replies with an honest "temporarily unavailable"
message and links to the Help Center. It never invents an answer.

## Analytics (all optional)

| Variable | Public? | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID` | public | GA4. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY` | public | PostHog project key. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST` | public | Defaults to `https://eu.i.posthog.com`. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` | public | Sentry DSN. |

When a key is absent the corresponding script is not loaded at all. A DSN is
write-only by design; keep the auth token out of the client config.

## Health check

`GET /api/health` returns a per-integration readiness report with **no secret
values** — only whether each key is present.